      "title": "Modeling Inhibited Growth"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "61efd521-6ce2-511b-be13-f0d19898bdf3",
      ":question/problem": "The growth of the number of deer in a protected forest is directly proportional to the difference between its maximum capacity and its current population. Let $N(t)$ be the number of deer, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in years. If the maximum capacity is $20$ deer, which differential equation models this population? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "5bcd1af6-8381-5d5c-9861-7106a182778d",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "4cf9edcc-e6fe-50ca-8462-fdf5d6c227a4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=kN(20-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "f3519198-5219-56d4-87ed-600e1484795c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(20-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "5a374769-1f59-5cbb-abfa-58c98f249905",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k(20+N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c6d59472-3214-5547-afe1-7ac50c2a90ef",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k(20-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "74e612be-7e9a-5a9d-a71d-10a9e8357378",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k{N}^{2}(20-N)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "f3519198-5219-56d4-87ed-600e1484795c"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate of change is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-N),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity and $k>0$.\n\nHere $a=20$ deer, so\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(20-N).\n$$"
    },
